{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Hi6kM5VtyCzAEam5Uk2uxH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity + R&D control system built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no database). Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose** â€” It's a personal productivity system whose source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, plus archives like `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). No DB, no binary formats â€” everything stays readable/editable from any CLI or editor.\n\n- **What it does (task layer)** â€” Manages a task lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) with priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields. You drive it either through a browser dashboard (`anchor_gui.py`, a stdlib-only local HTTP server on `localhost:8777`) or a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py` â€” done/cancel/save/restore/add/capture). The GUI writes changes straight back to the markdown and logs them.\n\n- **What it does (R&D layer)** â€” Layered on top is a \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D work (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). Each project gets a window where lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) show their most-recent session as a status-lit tile that expands into an inline panel pairing a cached summary with a **real, resizable terminal** (xterm.js over a Windows ConPTY/`pywinpty` backend). It supports git-worktree-isolated sessions, an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cost/token/time rollups, and type-aware deliverable launches.\n\n- **What it ships** â€” `anchor_gui.py` (the running app/web server), `anchor.py` (CLI engine + static `dashboard.html` generator), `anchor_healthcheck.py` (a daily 5 AM self-test that walks every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, fully stubbed), a set of R&D backend modules (`pty_manager`, `session_registry`, `worktrees`, `terminal_session`, `summarizer`, `effort_history`, `deliverables`, etc.), vendored frontend assets (xterm.js, anchor-term, GWL brand mark), and the markdown data files themselves.\n\n- **Runtime/constraints** â€” Runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`. Python **stdlib-only** with exactly **one** declared exception (`pywinpty`, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py` only, for the terminal subsystem, which degrades gracefully if absent). Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nThese are drawn from the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North Star / design docs; I haven't independently re-verified each module against the current source."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25235,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25235},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a117753e-cccb-4d9b-902e-30301034e6d4","uuid":"5427ca4c-fccf-4073-8976-6f168b9e3d33","request_id":"req_011Cc2JTZCup8RAWAAensRKg"}
